<phyphox version="1.20" locale="en">
    <title>Earth rotation (LSM6DSR)</title>
    <category>phyphox:mini experiments</category>
    <color>ADEBB3</color>
    <description>Measures the rotation rate of the Earth with the LSM6DSR gyroscope of a phyphox:mini. The gyroscope runs at its most sensitive range (125 °/s). Because the Earth signal is about the size of a single sensor bit, the bias is removed by an ABBA reversal: measure flat, turn the phyphox:mini upside down, measure, turn it back and measure again. The Earth signal changes sign with the flip, the sensor bias does not.</description>
    <translations>
        <translation locale="de">
            <title>Erdrotation (LSM6DSR)</title>
            <category>phyphox:mini Experimente</category>
            <description>Misst die Drehrate der Erde mit dem LSM6DSR-Gyroskop eines phyphox:mini. Das Gyroskop läuft im empfindlichsten Messbereich (125 °/s). Da das Erdsignal etwa so groß ist wie ein einzelnes Sensorbit, wird der Nullpunktfehler über eine ABBA-Umkehr entfernt: flach messen, phyphox:mini umdrehen, messen, zurückdrehen und nochmal messen. Das Erdsignal wechselt beim Umdrehen das Vorzeichen, der Sensor-Offset nicht.</description>
            <string original="Measurement">Messung</string>
            <string original="Put the phyphox:mini on a table that does not vibrate, start the measurement and do not touch it during a measuring phase. Phase 1 = settle, 2 = flat (A1), 3 = TURN OVER, 4 = upside down (B), 5 = TURN BACK, 6 = flat (A2), 7 = done. Only turn the phyphox:mini while the phase number is 3 or 5.">Den phyphox:mini auf einen erschütterungsfreien Tisch legen, die Messung starten und ihn während einer Messphase nicht berühren. Phase 1 = beruhigen, 2 = flach (A1), 3 = UMDREHEN, 4 = kopfüber (B), 5 = ZURÜCKDREHEN, 6 = flach (A2), 7 = fertig. Nur dann umdrehen, wenn die Phasennummer 3 oder 5 ist.</string>
            <string original="Elapsed time">Verstrichene Zeit</string>
            <string original="Phase">Phase</string>
            <string original="Next step in">Nächster Schritt in</string>
            <string original="The two steps in the live curve are the flips. Between them the curve has to be flat and quiet - every bump ruins the average.">Die beiden Stufen in der Live-Kurve sind die Umdrehungen. Dazwischen muss die Kurve flach und ruhig sein – jeder Stoß verdirbt den Mittelwert.</string>
            <string original="Gyroscope, all axes">Gyroskop, alle Achsen</string>
            <string original="Earth rotation rate">Erdrotationsrate</string>
            <string original="Expected">Erwartet</string>
            <string original="Deviation">Abweichung</string>
            <string original="Result">Ergebnis</string>
            <string original="The headline value uses the accelerometer to find out which way is up, so the phyphox:mini does not have to lie perfectly flat and you do not have to know how the board is mounted inside.">Der Hauptwert ermittelt die Lotrechte aus dem Beschleunigungssensor. Der phyphox:mini muss deshalb nicht exakt waagerecht liegen, und du musst nicht wissen, wie die Platine im Gehäuse verbaut ist.</string>
            <string original="Length of day">Tageslänge</string>
            <string original="Reversal difference per axis. The axis that pointed up shows the full signal, the other two should be near zero. Expected for the vertical axis: 2 * 0.00418 °/s * sin(latitude).">Umkehrdifferenz je Achse. Die Achse, die nach oben zeigte, liefert das volle Signal, die beiden anderen sollten nahe null liegen. Erwartet für die lotrechte Achse: 2 · 0,00418 °/s · sin(Breitengrad).</string>
            <string original="Reversal difference X">Umkehrdifferenz X</string>
            <string original="Reversal difference Y">Umkehrdifferenz Y</string>
            <string original="Reversal difference Z">Umkehrdifferenz Z</string>
            <string original="Projected onto vertical">Auf die Lotrechte projiziert</string>
            <string original="Orientation during phase A1, measured by the accelerometer. The axis near 9.81 was pointing up or down.">Ausrichtung während Phase A1, gemessen mit dem Beschleunigungssensor. Die Achse nahe 9,81 zeigte nach oben oder unten.</string>
            <string original="Acceleration X">Beschleunigung X</string>
            <string original="Acceleration Y">Beschleunigung Y</string>
            <string original="Acceleration Z">Beschleunigung Z</string>
            <string original="Samples per window. If one of these is zero or much smaller than expected (rate times window length), the connection dropped packets and the result is not trustworthy.">Samples pro Fenster. Ist einer davon null oder deutlich kleiner als erwartet (Rate mal Fensterlänge), hat die Verbindung Pakete verloren und das Ergebnis ist nicht belastbar.</string>
            <string original="Samples A1">Samples A1</string>
            <string original="Samples B">Samples B</string>
            <string original="Samples A2">Samples A2</string>
            <string original="Raw data">Rohdaten</string>
            <string original="Gyroscope X">Gyroskop X</string>
            <string original="Gyroscope Y">Gyroskop Y</string>
            <string original="Gyroscope Z">Gyroskop Z</string>
            <string original="Settings">Einstellungen</string>
            <string original="Set your latitude before starting. The vertical component of the Earth rotation is proportional to sin(latitude), so without it the result cannot be scaled correctly. Southern hemisphere: use a negative value.">Den Breitengrad vor dem Start eintragen. Die lotrechte Komponente der Erdrotation ist proportional zu sin(Breitengrad), ohne ihn lässt sich das Ergebnis nicht richtig skalieren. Südhalbkugel: negativen Wert eintragen.</string>
            <string original="Latitude">Breitengrad</string>
            <string original="Window length per measuring phase. Longer windows average away more noise but collect more thermal drift. The phase B window is twice this value, so the total run is 3 * pause + 4 * window.">Fensterlänge je Messphase. Längere Fenster mitteln mehr Rauschen weg, sammeln aber mehr thermische Drift an. Das B-Fenster ist doppelt so lang, der ganze Durchlauf dauert also 3 · Pause + 4 · Fensterlänge.</string>
            <string original="Window length">Fensterlänge</string>
            <string original="Pause for turning">Pause zum Umdrehen</string>
            <string original="Resulting schedule (seconds after start): A1 from b1 to b2, turn over, B from b3 to b4, turn back, A2 from b5 to b6.">Daraus ergibt sich folgender Ablauf (Sekunden nach dem Start): A1 von b1 bis b2, umdrehen, B von b3 bis b4, zurückdrehen, A2 von b5 bis b6.</string>
            <string original="A1 start">A1 Start</string>
            <string original="A1 end / turn over">A1 Ende / umdrehen</string>
            <string original="B start">B Start</string>
            <string original="B end / turn back">B Ende / zurückdrehen</string>
            <string original="A2 start">A2 Start</string>
            <string original="A2 end / done">A2 Ende / fertig</string>
            <string original="Gyr time (s)">Gyr Zeit (s)</string>
            <string original="Acc time (s)">Acc Zeit (s)</string>
            <string original="Latitude (°)">Breitengrad (°)</string>
            <string original="Window length (s)">Fensterlänge (s)</string>
            <string original="Mean A1 X">Mittel A1 X</string>
            <string original="Mean A1 Y">Mittel A1 Y</string>
            <string original="Mean A1 Z">Mittel A1 Z</string>
            <string original="Mean B X">Mittel B X</string>
            <string original="Mean B Y">Mittel B Y</string>
            <string original="Mean B Z">Mittel B Z</string>
            <string original="Mean A2 X">Mittel A2 X</string>
            <string original="Mean A2 Y">Mittel A2 Y</string>
            <string original="Mean A2 Z">Mittel A2 Z</string>
            <string original="Reversal difference X (°/s)">Umkehrdifferenz X (°/s)</string>
            <string original="Reversal difference Y (°/s)">Umkehrdifferenz Y (°/s)</string>
            <string original="Reversal difference Z (°/s)">Umkehrdifferenz Z (°/s)</string>
            <string original="Projected (°/s)">Projiziert (°/s)</string>
            <string original="Earth rotation (°/s)">Erdrotation (°/s)</string>
            <string original="Earth rotation (°/h)">Erdrotation (°/h)</string>
            <string original="Length of day (h)">Tageslänge (h)</string>
            <string original="Deviation (%)">Abweichung (%)</string>
        </translation>
    </translations>

    <data-containers>
        <!-- user settings -->
        <container size="1" init="51">latitude</container>
        <container size="1" init="45">seg</container>
        <container size="1" init="10">gap</container>
        <container size="1" init="0.00417807">omega_ref</container>

        <!-- phase boundaries, derived from seg and gap -->
        <container size="1">b1</container>
        <container size="1">b2</container>
        <container size="1">b3</container>
        <container size="1">b4</container>
        <container size="1">b5</container>
        <container size="1">b6</container>

        <!-- clock -->
        <container size="1">t_now</container>
        <container size="1">phase</container>
        <container size="1">t_next</container>

        <!-- raw BLE streams -->
        <container size="0">gyr_t</container>
        <container size="0">gyr_x</container>
        <container size="0">gyr_y</container>
        <container size="0">gyr_z</container>
        <container size="0">acc_t</container>
        <container size="0">acc_x</container>
        <container size="0">acc_y</container>
        <container size="0">acc_z</container>

        <!-- windowed data -->
        <container size="0">a1_t</container>
        <container size="0">a1_x</container>
        <container size="0">a1_y</container>
        <container size="0">a1_z</container>
        <container size="0">bb_t</container>
        <container size="0">bb_x</container>
        <container size="0">bb_y</container>
        <container size="0">bb_z</container>
        <container size="0">a2_t</container>
        <container size="0">a2_x</container>
        <container size="0">a2_y</container>
        <container size="0">a2_z</container>
        <container size="0">ac_t</container>
        <container size="0">ac_x</container>
        <container size="0">ac_y</container>
        <container size="0">ac_z</container>

        <!-- window averages -->
        <container size="1">m_a1x</container>
        <container size="1">m_a1y</container>
        <container size="1">m_a1z</container>
        <container size="1">m_bx</container>
        <container size="1">m_by</container>
        <container size="1">m_bz</container>
        <container size="1">m_a2x</container>
        <container size="1">m_a2y</container>
        <container size="1">m_a2z</container>
        <container size="1">m_ax</container>
        <container size="1">m_ay</container>
        <container size="1">m_az</container>

        <!-- sample counts, for checking that the windows were actually filled -->
        <container size="1">n_a1</container>
        <container size="1">n_bb</container>
        <container size="1">n_a2</container>

        <!-- results -->
        <container size="1">dw_x</container>
        <container size="1">dw_y</container>
        <container size="1">dw_z</container>
        <container size="1">a_abs</container>
        <container size="1">dw_proj</container>
        <container size="1">omega_dps</container>
        <container size="1">omega_dph</container>
        <container size="1">day_h</container>
        <container size="1">dev_pct</container>
    </data-containers>

    <input>
        <bluetooth id="phyphox:mini" name="phyphox:mini" mode="notification" mtu="247" subscribeOnStart="true">
            <!-- enable(acc+gyr), rate 104 Hz, acc 16 g, gyr 125 °/s, float, 15 samples per packet -->
            <config char="cddf1002-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" conversion="hexadecimal">03040102000F00</config>

            <output char="cddf1000-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" offset="0"  repeating="16" conversion="float32LittleEndian">gyr_t</output>
            <output char="cddf1000-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" offset="4"  repeating="16" conversion="float32LittleEndian">gyr_x</output>
            <output char="cddf1000-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" offset="8"  repeating="16" conversion="float32LittleEndian">gyr_y</output>
            <output char="cddf1000-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" offset="12" repeating="16" conversion="float32LittleEndian">gyr_z</output>

            <output char="cddf1001-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" offset="0"  repeating="16" conversion="float32LittleEndian">acc_t</output>
            <output char="cddf1001-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" offset="4"  repeating="16" conversion="float32LittleEndian">acc_x</output>
            <output char="cddf1001-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" offset="8"  repeating="16" conversion="float32LittleEndian">acc_y</output>
            <output char="cddf1001-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" offset="12" repeating="16" conversion="float32LittleEndian">acc_z</output>
        </bluetooth>
    </input>

    <views>
        <view label="Measurement">
            <info label="Put the phyphox:mini on a table that does not vibrate, start the measurement and do not touch it during a measuring phase. Phase 1 = settle, 2 = flat (A1), 3 = TURN OVER, 4 = upside down (B), 5 = TURN BACK, 6 = flat (A2), 7 = done. Only turn the phyphox:mini while the phase number is 3 or 5."/>
            <value label="Elapsed time" size="1" precision="1" scientific="false" factor="1" unit="s">
                <input>t_now</input>
            </value>
            <value label="Phase" size="1" precision="0" scientific="false" factor="1">
                <input>phase</input>
            </value>
            <value label="Next step in" size="1" precision="0" scientific="false" factor="1" unit="s">
                <input>t_next</input>
            </value>
            <separator height="0.5"/>
            <info label="The two steps in the live curve are the flips. Between them the curve has to be flat and quiet - every bump ruins the average."/>
            <graph label="Gyroscope, all axes" timeOnX="true" labelX="t" unitX="s" labelY="ω" unitY="°/s" partialUpdate="true" hideTimeMarkers="true">
                <input axis="x">gyr_t</input>
                <input axis="y">gyr_z</input>
            </graph>
            <separator height="0.5"/>
            <value label="Earth rotation rate" size="1" precision="5" scientific="false" factor="1" unit="°/s">
                <input>omega_dps</input>
            </value>
            <value label="Expected" size="1" precision="5" scientific="false" factor="1" unit="°/s">
                <input>omega_ref</input>
            </value>
            <value label="Deviation" size="1" precision="1" scientific="false" factor="1" unit="%">
                <input>dev_pct</input>
            </value>
        </view>

        <view label="Result">
            <info label="The headline value uses the accelerometer to find out which way is up, so the phyphox:mini does not have to lie perfectly flat and you do not have to know how the board is mounted inside."/>
            <value label="Earth rotation rate" size="1" precision="5" scientific="false" factor="1" unit="°/s">
                <input>omega_dps</input>
            </value>
            <value label="Earth rotation rate" size="1" precision="3" scientific="false" factor="1" unit="°/h">
                <input>omega_dph</input>
            </value>
            <value label="Length of day" size="1" precision="3" scientific="false" factor="1" unit="h">
                <input>day_h</input>
            </value>
            <value label="Deviation" size="1" precision="1" scientific="false" factor="1" unit="%">
                <input>dev_pct</input>
            </value>
            <separator height="0.5"/>
            <info label="Reversal difference per axis. The axis that pointed up shows the full signal, the other two should be near zero. Expected for the vertical axis: 2 * 0.00418 °/s * sin(latitude)."/>
            <value label="Reversal difference X" size="1" precision="5" scientific="false" factor="1" unit="°/s">
                <input>dw_x</input>
            </value>
            <value label="Reversal difference Y" size="1" precision="5" scientific="false" factor="1" unit="°/s">
                <input>dw_y</input>
            </value>
            <value label="Reversal difference Z" size="1" precision="5" scientific="false" factor="1" unit="°/s">
                <input>dw_z</input>
            </value>
            <value label="Projected onto vertical" size="1" precision="5" scientific="false" factor="1" unit="°/s">
                <input>dw_proj</input>
            </value>
            <separator height="0.5"/>
            <info label="Orientation during phase A1, measured by the accelerometer. The axis near 9.81 was pointing up or down."/>
            <value label="Acceleration X" size="1" precision="2" scientific="false" factor="1" unit="m/s²">
                <input>m_ax</input>
            </value>
            <value label="Acceleration Y" size="1" precision="2" scientific="false" factor="1" unit="m/s²">
                <input>m_ay</input>
            </value>
            <value label="Acceleration Z" size="1" precision="2" scientific="false" factor="1" unit="m/s²">
                <input>m_az</input>
            </value>
            <separator height="0.5"/>
            <info label="Samples per window. If one of these is zero or much smaller than expected (rate times window length), the connection dropped packets and the result is not trustworthy."/>
            <value label="Samples A1" size="1" precision="0" scientific="false" factor="1">
                <input>n_a1</input>
            </value>
            <value label="Samples B" size="1" precision="0" scientific="false" factor="1">
                <input>n_bb</input>
            </value>
            <value label="Samples A2" size="1" precision="0" scientific="false" factor="1">
                <input>n_a2</input>
            </value>
        </view>

        <view label="Raw data">
            <graph label="Gyroscope X" timeOnX="true" labelX="t" unitX="s" labelY="ω" unitY="°/s" partialUpdate="true" hideTimeMarkers="true">
                <input axis="x">gyr_t</input>
                <input axis="y">gyr_x</input>
            </graph>
            <graph label="Gyroscope Y" timeOnX="true" labelX="t" unitX="s" labelY="ω" unitY="°/s" partialUpdate="true" hideTimeMarkers="true">
                <input axis="x">gyr_t</input>
                <input axis="y">gyr_y</input>
            </graph>
            <graph label="Gyroscope Z" timeOnX="true" labelX="t" unitX="s" labelY="ω" unitY="°/s" partialUpdate="true" hideTimeMarkers="true">
                <input axis="x">gyr_t</input>
                <input axis="y">gyr_z</input>
            </graph>
            <graph label="Acceleration Z" timeOnX="true" labelX="t" unitX="s" labelY="a" unitY="m/s²" partialUpdate="true" hideTimeMarkers="true">
                <input axis="x">acc_t</input>
                <input axis="y">acc_z</input>
            </graph>
        </view>

        <view label="Settings">
            <info label="Set your latitude before starting. The vertical component of the Earth rotation is proportional to sin(latitude), so without it the result cannot be scaled correctly. Southern hemisphere: use a negative value."/>
            <edit label="Latitude" signed="true" decimal="true" min="-90" max="90" unit="°" factor="1" default="51">
                <output>latitude</output>
            </edit>
            <separator height="0.5"/>
            <info label="Window length per measuring phase. Longer windows average away more noise but collect more thermal drift. The phase B window is twice this value, so the total run is 3 * pause + 4 * window."/>
            <edit label="Window length" signed="false" decimal="false" min="10" max="600" unit="s" factor="1" default="45">
                <output>seg</output>
            </edit>
            <edit label="Pause for turning" signed="false" decimal="false" min="3" max="60" unit="s" factor="1" default="10">
                <output>gap</output>
            </edit>
            <separator height="0.5"/>
            <info label="Resulting schedule (seconds after start): A1 from b1 to b2, turn over, B from b3 to b4, turn back, A2 from b5 to b6."/>
            <value label="A1 start" size="1" precision="0" scientific="false" factor="1" unit="s">
                <input>b1</input>
            </value>
            <value label="A1 end / turn over" size="1" precision="0" scientific="false" factor="1" unit="s">
                <input>b2</input>
            </value>
            <value label="B start" size="1" precision="0" scientific="false" factor="1" unit="s">
                <input>b3</input>
            </value>
            <value label="B end / turn back" size="1" precision="0" scientific="false" factor="1" unit="s">
                <input>b4</input>
            </value>
            <value label="A2 start" size="1" precision="0" scientific="false" factor="1" unit="s">
                <input>b5</input>
            </value>
            <value label="A2 end / done" size="1" precision="0" scientific="false" factor="1" unit="s">
                <input>b6</input>
            </value>
        </view>
    </views>

    <analysis sleep="1">
        <!-- phase boundaries from the two settings -->
        <formula formula="[1]">
            <input keep="true">gap</input>
            <output keep="true">b1</output>
        </formula>
        <formula formula="[1]+[2]">
            <input keep="true">gap</input>
            <input keep="true">seg</input>
            <output keep="true">b2</output>
        </formula>
        <formula formula="2*[1]+[2]">
            <input keep="true">gap</input>
            <input keep="true">seg</input>
            <output keep="true">b3</output>
        </formula>
        <formula formula="2*[1]+3*[2]">
            <input keep="true">gap</input>
            <input keep="true">seg</input>
            <output keep="true">b4</output>
        </formula>
        <formula formula="3*[1]+3*[2]">
            <input keep="true">gap</input>
            <input keep="true">seg</input>
            <output keep="true">b5</output>
        </formula>
        <formula formula="3*[1]+4*[2]">
            <input keep="true">gap</input>
            <input keep="true">seg</input>
            <output keep="true">b6</output>
        </formula>

        <!-- experiment clock, phase number and countdown to the next boundary -->
        <timer>
            <output as="out">t_now</output>
        </timer>
        <formula formula="1+heaviside([1]-[2])+heaviside([1]-[3])+heaviside([1]-[4])+heaviside([1]-[5])+heaviside([1]-[6])+heaviside([1]-[7])">
            <input keep="true">t_now</input>
            <input keep="true">b1</input>
            <input keep="true">b2</input>
            <input keep="true">b3</input>
            <input keep="true">b4</input>
            <input keep="true">b5</input>
            <input keep="true">b6</input>
            <output keep="true">phase</output>
        </formula>
        <formula formula="max([2]+([3]-[2])*heaviside([1]-[2])+([4]-[3])*heaviside([1]-[3])+([5]-[4])*heaviside([1]-[4])+([6]-[5])*heaviside([1]-[5])+([7]-[6])*heaviside([1]-[6])-[1],0)">
            <input keep="true">t_now</input>
            <input keep="true">b1</input>
            <input keep="true">b2</input>
            <input keep="true">b3</input>
            <input keep="true">b4</input>
            <input keep="true">b5</input>
            <input keep="true">b6</input>
            <output keep="true">t_next</output>
        </formula>

        <!-- cut the three measuring windows out of the gyroscope stream -->
        <rangefilter>
            <input keep="true">gyr_t</input>
            <input as="min" keep="true">b1</input>
            <input as="max" keep="true">b2</input>
            <input keep="true">gyr_x</input>
            <input keep="true">gyr_y</input>
            <input keep="true">gyr_z</input>
            <output>a1_t</output>
            <output>a1_x</output>
            <output>a1_y</output>
            <output>a1_z</output>
        </rangefilter>
        <rangefilter>
            <input keep="true">gyr_t</input>
            <input as="min" keep="true">b3</input>
            <input as="max" keep="true">b4</input>
            <input keep="true">gyr_x</input>
            <input keep="true">gyr_y</input>
            <input keep="true">gyr_z</input>
            <output>bb_t</output>
            <output>bb_x</output>
            <output>bb_y</output>
            <output>bb_z</output>
        </rangefilter>
        <rangefilter>
            <input keep="true">gyr_t</input>
            <input as="min" keep="true">b5</input>
            <input as="max" keep="true">b6</input>
            <input keep="true">gyr_x</input>
            <input keep="true">gyr_y</input>
            <input keep="true">gyr_z</input>
            <output>a2_t</output>
            <output>a2_x</output>
            <output>a2_y</output>
            <output>a2_z</output>
        </rangefilter>
        <!-- accelerometer during A1, used as the "which way is up" reference -->
        <rangefilter>
            <input keep="true">acc_t</input>
            <input as="min" keep="true">b1</input>
            <input as="max" keep="true">b2</input>
            <input keep="true">acc_x</input>
            <input keep="true">acc_y</input>
            <input keep="true">acc_z</input>
            <output>ac_t</output>
            <output>ac_x</output>
            <output>ac_y</output>
            <output>ac_z</output>
        </rangefilter>

        <!-- how many samples actually arrived per window -->
        <count>
            <input keep="true">a1_t</input>
            <output>n_a1</output>
        </count>
        <count>
            <input keep="true">bb_t</input>
            <output>n_bb</output>
        </count>
        <count>
            <input keep="true">a2_t</input>
            <output>n_a2</output>
        </count>

        <!-- window averages -->
        <average>
            <input as="buffer" keep="true">a1_x</input>
            <output as="average" keep="true">m_a1x</output>
        </average>
        <average>
            <input as="buffer" keep="true">a1_y</input>
            <output as="average" keep="true">m_a1y</output>
        </average>
        <average>
            <input as="buffer" keep="true">a1_z</input>
            <output as="average" keep="true">m_a1z</output>
        </average>
        <average>
            <input as="buffer" keep="true">bb_x</input>
            <output as="average" keep="true">m_bx</output>
        </average>
        <average>
            <input as="buffer" keep="true">bb_y</input>
            <output as="average" keep="true">m_by</output>
        </average>
        <average>
            <input as="buffer" keep="true">bb_z</input>
            <output as="average" keep="true">m_bz</output>
        </average>
        <average>
            <input as="buffer" keep="true">a2_x</input>
            <output as="average" keep="true">m_a2x</output>
        </average>
        <average>
            <input as="buffer" keep="true">a2_y</input>
            <output as="average" keep="true">m_a2y</output>
        </average>
        <average>
            <input as="buffer" keep="true">a2_z</input>
            <output as="average" keep="true">m_a2z</output>
        </average>
        <average>
            <input as="buffer" keep="true">ac_x</input>
            <output as="average" keep="true">m_ax</output>
        </average>
        <average>
            <input as="buffer" keep="true">ac_y</input>
            <output as="average" keep="true">m_ay</output>
        </average>
        <average>
            <input as="buffer" keep="true">ac_z</input>
            <output as="average" keep="true">m_az</output>
        </average>

        <!-- ABBA reversal difference per axis: (A1 + A2)/2 - B -->
        <formula formula="([1]+[2])/2-[3]">
            <input keep="true">m_a1x</input>
            <input keep="true">m_a2x</input>
            <input keep="true">m_bx</input>
            <output keep="true">dw_x</output>
        </formula>
        <formula formula="([1]+[2])/2-[3]">
            <input keep="true">m_a1y</input>
            <input keep="true">m_a2y</input>
            <input keep="true">m_by</input>
            <output keep="true">dw_y</output>
        </formula>
        <formula formula="([1]+[2])/2-[3]">
            <input keep="true">m_a1z</input>
            <input keep="true">m_a2z</input>
            <input keep="true">m_bz</input>
            <output keep="true">dw_z</output>
        </formula>

        <!-- project the reversal difference onto the vertical found by the accelerometer -->
        <formula formula="sqrt([1]^2+[2]^2+[3]^2)">
            <input keep="true">m_ax</input>
            <input keep="true">m_ay</input>
            <input keep="true">m_az</input>
            <output keep="true">a_abs</output>
        </formula>
        <formula formula="([1]*[4]+[2]*[5]+[3]*[6])/[7]">
            <input keep="true">dw_x</input>
            <input keep="true">dw_y</input>
            <input keep="true">dw_z</input>
            <input keep="true">m_ax</input>
            <input keep="true">m_ay</input>
            <input keep="true">m_az</input>
            <input keep="true">a_abs</input>
            <output keep="true">dw_proj</output>
        </formula>

        <!-- the reversal difference is twice the vertical component: 2 * Omega * sin(latitude) -->
        <formula formula="abs([1])/(2*abs(sin([2]*3.141592653589793/180)))">
            <input keep="true">dw_proj</input>
            <input keep="true">latitude</input>
            <output keep="true">omega_dps</output>
        </formula>
        <formula formula="[1]*3600">
            <input keep="true">omega_dps</input>
            <output keep="true">omega_dph</output>
        </formula>
        <formula formula="360/[1]/3600">
            <input keep="true">omega_dps</input>
            <output keep="true">day_h</output>
        </formula>
        <formula formula="([1]-[2])/[2]*100">
            <input keep="true">omega_dps</input>
            <input keep="true">omega_ref</input>
            <output keep="true">dev_pct</output>
        </formula>
    </analysis>

    <export>
        <set name="Raw data">
            <data name="Gyr time (s)">gyr_t</data>
            <data name="Gyr X (°/s)">gyr_x</data>
            <data name="Gyr Y (°/s)">gyr_y</data>
            <data name="Gyr Z (°/s)">gyr_z</data>
            <data name="Acc time (s)">acc_t</data>
            <data name="Acc X (m/s²)">acc_x</data>
            <data name="Acc Y (m/s²)">acc_y</data>
            <data name="Acc Z (m/s²)">acc_z</data>
        </set>
        <set name="Result">
            <data name="Latitude (°)">latitude</data>
            <data name="Window length (s)">seg</data>
            <data name="Mean A1 X">m_a1x</data>
            <data name="Mean A1 Y">m_a1y</data>
            <data name="Mean A1 Z">m_a1z</data>
            <data name="Mean B X">m_bx</data>
            <data name="Mean B Y">m_by</data>
            <data name="Mean B Z">m_bz</data>
            <data name="Mean A2 X">m_a2x</data>
            <data name="Mean A2 Y">m_a2y</data>
            <data name="Mean A2 Z">m_a2z</data>
            <data name="Reversal difference X (°/s)">dw_x</data>
            <data name="Reversal difference Y (°/s)">dw_y</data>
            <data name="Reversal difference Z (°/s)">dw_z</data>
            <data name="Projected (°/s)">dw_proj</data>
            <data name="Earth rotation (°/s)">omega_dps</data>
            <data name="Earth rotation (°/h)">omega_dph</data>
            <data name="Length of day (h)">day_h</data>
            <data name="Deviation (%)">dev_pct</data>
            <data name="Samples A1">n_a1</data>
            <data name="Samples B">n_bb</data>
            <data name="Samples A2">n_a2</data>
        </set>
    </export>
</phyphox>
